{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"5abb42ac-c960-48c0-82ed-6bd8b88c3f6c","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The cause of the failure has been identified, fixed in [run-vibe.sh](file:///tmp/h-UzMjxB/run-vibe.sh), verified, and documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-UzMjxB/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Cause \u0026 Fix\n- **Root Cause**: Mistral Vibe CLI attempts to retrieve `MISTRAL_API_KEY` from the macOS Keychain at startup via `/usr/bin/security` whenever it is missing from the environment, even when an alternative provider (OpenRouter) is configured. Because [run-vibe.sh](file:///tmp/h-UzMjxB/run-vibe.sh) runs Vibe via `env -i` without `MISTRAL_API_KEY`, and [agent.sb](file:///tmp/h-UzMjxB/agent.sb) explicitly denies executing `/usr/bin/security`, the process failed immediately with exit code 2: `[Errno 1] Operation not permitted: '/usr/bin/security'`.\n- **Fix**: Added `MISTRAL_API_KEY=\"unused\"` to the `env -i` parameter list in [run-vibe.sh](file:///tmp/h-UzMjxB/run-vibe.sh). This prevents Vibe from querying the Keychain while leaving the sandbox restrictions in [agent.sb](file:///tmp/h-UzMjxB/agent.sb) intact.\n- **Verification**: Executed [run-vibe.sh](file:///tmp/h-UzMjxB/run-vibe.sh); Vibe now starts up properly, writes its export output, and reaches the provider without attempting Keychain access. Tested that `/usr/bin/security` remains blocked inside [agent.sb](file:///tmp/h-UzMjxB/agent.sb).\n","duration_seconds":54.142603,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":166491,"output_tokens":1982,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":168473}}}
